# The app selects its workspace at runtime from the URL (?workspace=<slug>)
# or authenticated memberships. Project pages can select ?projectId=<uuid>.
# No build-time workspace setting is required.

# ── Playwright / E2E auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required to run E2E tests against a Cloudflare Access-protected deployment.
# Create a CF Access service token scoped to the projektor application in the
# Cloudflare dashboard and paste the values below.  Never commit real values.

# URL of the deployed dev instance (e.g. https://dev.your-instance.workers.dev)
# E2E_BASE_URL=

# Optional email for the test member provisioned by globalSetup.
# Defaults to a unique address in the generated isolated E2E workspace.
# E2E_MEMBER_EMAIL=

# Optional real workspace-scoped token for the invited test member.
# Confinement tests require both E2E_MEMBER_TOKEN and E2E_MEMBER_EMAIL.
# E2E_MEMBER_TOKEN=

# globalSetup generates the test workspace and project IDs in E2EContext.
# Browser tests select them through URLs, not blanket workspace headers.

# Cloudflare Access service token - injected as CF-Access-Client-Id /
# CF-Access-Client-Secret on every Playwright browser request.
# CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID=
# CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET=

# App bearer token - injected as Authorization: Bearer <token>.
# Use an existing user-scoped API token or create a dedicated test token.
# PROJEKTOR_API_TOKEN=
